# The Circagraph server for macOS (#116), published to circagraph/homebrew-tap by releases
# (scripts/homebrew-formula.mjs renders this template). Until 0.30 it was openchronology-server;
# the tap's formula_renames.json moves those installations here, and post_install moves their
# configuration.
class CircagraphServer < Formula
  desc "Exact timelines, shared on your terms: the Circagraph platform server"
  homepage "https://github.com/circagraph/timeline-app"
  url "@URL@"
  version "@VERSION@"
  sha256 "@SHA256@"
  license "GPL-3.0-only"

  depends_on "cmake" => :build
  depends_on "pkgconf" => :build
  depends_on "rust" => :build
  depends_on "gmp"
  depends_on "node@24"
  depends_on "postgresql@17"
  depends_on "sqlite"

  uses_from_macos "python" => :build

  # The exact-rational type for PostgreSQL, pinned as the other packages pin it.
  resource "pgmp" do
    url "https://codeload.github.com/dvarrazzo/pgmp/tar.gz/1849585416f2bc3d070bf8cef6a659907687ec7f"
    version "1.1-1849585"
    sha256 "@PGMP_SHA256@"
  end

  def postgresql
    Formula["postgresql@17"]
  end

  def node
    Formula["node@24"].opt_bin/"node"
  end

  def install
    # The SQLite converter, from the crates vendored in the platform archive.
    cd "native" do
      system "cargo", "build", "--manifest-path", "native-store/Cargo.toml", "--release",
             "--locked", "--offline", "--bin", "cg-convert"
    end
    # The platform (Next.js and the editor), laid out as the other packages lay it out.
    libexec.mkpath
    cp_r "lib/circagraph/.", libexec
    (libexec/"bin").install "native/native-store/target/release/cg-convert"
    # och-convert is the converter's name before the rename, which a configuration may name.
    (libexec/"bin").install_symlink "cg-convert" => "och-convert"
    # The launcher by its name before the rename, which the openchronology-server service that
    # an earlier installation started runs until circagraph-migrate replaces it.
    libexec.install_symlink "circagraph-server.mjs" => "openchronology-server.mjs"

    # pgmp, installed where Homebrew's postgresql@17 finds extensions (as pgvector is).
    resource("pgmp").stage do
      system "sh", "-c", "python3 tools/unmix.py < sql/pgmp.pysql > sql/pgmp--1.1.sql"
      system "sh", "-c", "python3 tools/sql2extension.py --extname pgmp sql/pgmp--1.1.sql " \
                         "> sql/pgmp--unpackaged--1.1.sql"
      pg_config = "PG_CONFIG=#{postgresql.opt_bin}/pg_config"
      system "make", pg_config, "with_llvm=no"
      system "make", "install", pg_config, "with_llvm=no",
             "pkglibdir=#{lib/postgresql.name}",
             "datadir=#{share/postgresql.name}",
             "docdir=#{doc}/pgmp"
      (doc/"pgmp").install "COPYING"
    end

    # Configuration templates, with this Mac's paths.
    (share/"circagraph").install "homebrew/circagraph.env" => "circagraph.env.example",
                                 "homebrew/syslog.env"     => "syslog.env.example",
                                 "homebrew/github.env"     => "github.env.example"
    inreplace share.glob("circagraph/*.example") do |s|
      s.gsub! "/etc/circagraph", "#{etc}/circagraph", audit_result: false
      # The GitHub receiver's state, beside the server's data.
      s.gsub! "/var/lib/circagraph-github", "#{var}/circagraph", audit_result: false
      s.gsub! "sudo systemctl restart circagraph", "brew services restart circagraph-server",
              audit_result: false
      # The mail, syslog and GitHub workers run as your launchd agents (circagraph-agent).
      s.gsub! "sudo systemctl enable --now circagraph-", "circagraph-agent start ",
              audit_result: false
      s.gsub! "sudo circagraph-", "circagraph-", audit_result: false
    end

    # The commands, pointing at this installation.
    commands = %w[circagraph-setup circagraph-migrate circagraph-reset-admin-password
                  cg-import-logs cg-import-github circagraph-mail circagraph-syslog
                  circagraph-github circagraph-agent]
    commands.each { |command| bin.install "homebrew/#{command}" }
    # Not every command names every path.
    inreplace commands.map { |command| bin/command } do |s|
      s.gsub! "@HOMEBREW_PREFIX@", HOMEBREW_PREFIX.to_s, audit_result: false
      s.gsub! "@LIBEXEC@", opt_libexec.to_s, audit_result: false
      s.gsub! "@NODE@", node.to_s, audit_result: false
      s.gsub! "@PG_BIN@", postgresql.opt_bin.to_s, audit_result: false
      s.gsub! "@PG_MAJOR@", postgresql.version.major.to_s, audit_result: false
    end

    # The commands' names before the rename (openchronology-*, och-import-*) still work.
    commands.each do |command|
      old = command.sub(/\Acircagraph-/, "openchronology-").sub(/\Acg-/, "och-")
      bin.install_symlink command => old
    end

    doc.install Dir["doc/*"], "homebrew/README.Homebrew"
  end

  def post_install
    # An installation of openchronology-server: its configuration, under the new names, with
    # links from the old ones. Its database, its state (var/openchronology) and its launchd
    # agents keep their names until circagraph-migrate moves the agents.
    old_config = etc/"openchronology"
    config = etc/"circagraph"
    if old_config.directory? && !old_config.symlink? && !config.exist?
      mv old_config, config
      ln_s "circagraph", old_config
    end
    if (config/"openchronology.env").file? && !(config/"openchronology.env").symlink? &&
       !(config/"circagraph.env").exist?
      mv config/"openchronology.env", config/"circagraph.env"
      ln_s "circagraph.env", config/"openchronology.env"
    end
    (var/"circagraph").mkpath
    (var/"log").mkpath
  end

  def caveats
    <<~EOS
      To finish the installation, run:
        circagraph-setup
      It starts PostgreSQL 17 (brew services) if it is not running, creates the circagraph
      database, and starts the server on http://localhost:5173.

      Configuration: #{etc}/circagraph/circagraph.env
      After upgrading, migrate the database: circagraph-migrate
      Upgrading from openchronology-server, circagraph-migrate also moves its service and
      launchd agents to their new names; the database keeps its name.
      More: #{HOMEBREW_PREFIX}/share/doc/circagraph-server/README.Homebrew
    EOS
  end

  service do
    run [Formula["node@24"].opt_bin/"node", opt_libexec/"circagraph-server.mjs"]
    environment_variables OCH_CONFIG: etc/"circagraph/circagraph.env",
                          NODE_ENV:   "production"
    keep_alive true
    working_dir opt_libexec
    log_path var/"log/circagraph.log"
    error_log_path var/"log/circagraph.log"
  end

  test do
    assert_match "Usage: cg-import-logs", shell_output("#{bin}/cg-import-logs --help")
    assert_match "Usage: cg-import-github", shell_output("#{bin}/cg-import-github --help")
    assert_match "Usage: cg-import-logs", shell_output("#{bin}/och-import-logs --help")
    assert_path_exists libexec/"bin/cg-convert"
    assert_path_exists libexec/"bin/och-convert"
    # pgmp loads in a scratch PostgreSQL 17 cluster.
    ENV["LC_ALL"] = "C"
    pg_ctl = postgresql.opt_bin/"pg_ctl"
    port = free_port
    system pg_ctl, "initdb", "-D", testpath/"data"
    (testpath/"data/postgresql.conf").write <<~EOS, mode: "a+"
      port = #{port}
      unix_socket_directories = '#{testpath}'
    EOS
    system pg_ctl, "start", "-D", testpath/"data", "-l", testpath/"log"
    begin
      output = shell_output("#{postgresql.opt_bin}/psql -h #{testpath} -p #{port} -Atc " \
                            "\"CREATE EXTENSION pgmp; SELECT '1/3'::mpq + '1/6'::mpq\" postgres")
      assert_match "1/2", output
    ensure
      system pg_ctl, "stop", "-D", testpath/"data"
    end
  end
end
